# FIRSTgo voice commands (Zippy push-to-talk). Copy to .env.local and restart Metro (npx expo start -c).
# Only the PROXY URL goes here — models and credentials live on the proxy, never in the app.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STT_URL = base URL of a voice proxy, NO trailing path
#   (the app POSTs to <url>/command and <url>/tts).
#
# Default: the LOCAL pipeline (Whisper STT + LaBSE intent + Piper TTS).
# Google Speech-to-Text is only a server-side fallback inside that pipeline — do not
# point the app at the Google proxy (8792) by default, because that costs money.
# Spoken replies always use Piper, never Google TTS.
#
#   Local Whisper + LaBSE + Piper (default):  http://127.0.0.1:8793
#   Google STT proxy (avoid as app default):  http://127.0.0.1:8792
#
# 127.0.0.1 works for web / iOS simulator on this box (Android emulator: 10.0.2.2).
# Developers on this box can leave EXPO_PUBLIC_STT_URL unset — the code default is 127.0.0.1:8793.
#
# Physical phones / release APKs: metro.config.js proxies /voice/* on the Expo dev server (8081)
# to 127.0.0.1:8793, so the EXISTING Expo tunnel reaches the pipeline. Public test base
# (no trailing slash; the app posts to <url>/command and <url>/tts):
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_STT_URL=https://yl0nisu-anonymous-8081.exp.direct/voice
# Requires `npx expo start --tunnel` running on this box and the 8793 pipeline up.
EXPO_PUBLIC_STT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8793
# Only if you deliberately want the Google proxy (billed):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_STT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8792

# "google" here means "HTTP /command client" (including the local 8793 stack).
# "sarvam" is a stub that throws "not configured".
EXPO_PUBLIC_STT_PROVIDER=google
